//! @generated by `cargo xtask codegen` from the `wasm-encoder` crate — DO NOT hand-edit.
//!
//! Every wasm / component-model byte the backend emits, EXTRACTED from `wasm-encoder` (the spec
//! byte encoder): the core opcode table, core + component valtype bytes, core + component section
//! ids, the two magic headers, and the functype form bytes. `codegen` encodes a one-off value
//! with `wasm-encoder` and reads the byte back, so nothing here is hand-transcribed. Regenerate
//! with `cargo xtask codegen`; `cargo xtask codegen --check` (a hard gate in `xtask check`) fails
//! if it drifts from the encoder. Plain data — no dependency, so it ships in the portable
//! compiler (the `wasm-encoder` oracle stays in xtask). The backend's serializer reads these
//! rather than baking a raw byte into the emit path.

